{
  "statement": "The SafetyAgent underscores the paramount importance of safety in autonomous driving. SAF-01 establishes a robust multi-layer safety architecture that is indispensable for collision protection and reliable operations. SAF-02 mandates Minimal Risk Maneuvers, ensuring the vehicle can safely navigate critical failures rather than stopping abruptly, which is vital for passenger safety. SAF-03 emphasizes continuous monitoring of the Operational Design Domain to mitigate risks. SAF-04 and SAF-05 focus on minimizing jerk and satisfying curvature constraints, preventing accidents during maneuvers. SAF-07 allows for relaxing smoothness constraints during emergencies, prioritizing safety over comfort, which is crucial in crisis situations. These requirements collectively ensure a reliable and safe autonomous driving system.",
  "conflicts_raised": [
    {
      "ids": ["EFF-07"],
      "type": "logical",
      "description": "EFF-07's emphasis on prioritizing smoothness during emergency maneuvers contradicts SAF-07's provision to relax smoothness constraints for safety."
    },
    {
      "ids": ["GRN-01", "EFF-01"],
      "type": "resource",
      "description": "The energy efficiency requirements of GRN-01 and EFF-01 may conflict with the need for immediate safety maneuvers outlined in SAF-02, potentially compromising safety."
    }
  ],
